#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Lists the dev commands.
cat <<'TEXT'
Nix-Manager dev commands

Environment
  direnv allow                 enter the dev shell automatically (.envrc -> use flake)
  nix develop                  or enter it by hand

Run
  ./scripts/run                        build, start the backend and one frontend window
  ./scripts/run -n 3                   ...three frontend windows on the same backend
  ./scripts/run -b                     backend only, in the foreground
  ./scripts/run -f                     only a frontend window, attached to a running dev backend
  ./scripts/run -r                     release build
  ./scripts/run -c DIR -H HOST         point the backend at a flake directory / nixosConfiguration

  The backend uses its own socket ($XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nix-manager-dev.sock), so it never
  takes over a real daemon's socket. The default target is /etc/nixos: rebuilds and
  updates are real, so use -c with a scratch flake while developing.

Build, check, test
  cargo build --workspace                                         client + frontends
  cargo build --manifest-path nix-backend-generic/Cargo.toml      backend (standalone crate)
  cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets
  cargo test --workspace
  cargo fmt --all                                                 client + frontends only
  cargo watch -x 'clippy --workspace --all-targets'               re-check on save
  cargo clean                                                     (and again with --manifest-path ...)

Talk to the backend directly
  S=$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nix-manager-dev.sock
  P="-import-path nix-backend-generic/proto -proto nix_backend.proto"
  grpcurl -plaintext -unix $P $S list caelestia.nixbackend.v1.NixBackend
  grpcurl -plaintext -unix $P -d '{}' $S caelestia.nixbackend.v1.NixBackend/GetFlakeStatus
  grpcurl -plaintext -unix $P -d '{}' $S caelestia.nixbackend.v1.NixBackend/Watch

Layout
  nix-backend-generic/    gRPC backend (standalone crate; owns proto/nix_backend.proto)
  nix-backend-client/     frontend-agnostic client library shared by every frontend
  nix-frontend-iced/      iced + mina GUI frontend

One backend serves any number of frontend instances at once: they all follow the same
operation through the backend's Watch stream, and only one update/rebuild runs at a time.

Environment variables
  NIX_BACKEND_SOCKET        socket to use
  NIX_BACKEND_CONFIG_DIR    flake directory (default /etc/nixos)
  NIX_BACKEND_HOST_NAME     host to build (default: this machine's hostname)
  RUST_LOG                  backend log filter (default info)
TEXT
